## The transition from NIS to NIS2

The NIS2 directive replaced the original NIS directive (EU) 2016/1148 on 18 October 2024. The most important difference is an extended scope:

- More sectors are covered, 18 in total compared to the previous 7
- A new classification of *essential* and *important* entities replaces the old division
- Clearer management responsibility and stricter sanction options
- Mandatory incident reporting within 24 hours

## In Swedish law

NIS2 was transposed through the Cybersecurity Act (2025:150), which replaces the Act (2018:1174) on information security for essential and digital services.
